diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 9f351fa6..c44c64ac 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -20,6 +20,12 @@ questions; `codex-dominant-adversarial-claude` is its mirror image. Installing
 Kogen into arbitrary projects and other harnesses are future work.
 The broader design remains a longer-term direction, open to change as Kogen develops.
 
+## Failure reports
+
+Every stopped Build with a tracking record writes one durable report at `.kogen/runtime/scenario-tracking/<build-id>/failure-report.json`. Reports include the stop category and class, failure signature and recurrence count, next action and optional command, candidate context, a control-relative record path, and the SHA-256 of the final record bytes. Reports use a same-directory temporary file and no-clobber publication.
+
+`mix kogen.candidates` shows a kept report's class, next action (and command when present), and report path. Candidates without a report show `report: none`.
+
 This repository is being opened quietly so the ongoing work and its history
 can be inspected. Kogen is Almir Sarajčić’s personal engineering project.
 
